rst:  chills, dehydration, fast breathing, fast heart rate, fever\n  Favours second: abnormal brainstem morphology, abnormal cell morphology, abnormal cerebellum morphology, abnormal conjugate eye movement, abnormal cortical gyration\n\nHypertriglyceridemia-Induced Acute Pancreatitis vs Idiopathic/Atypical Acute Pancreatitis:\n  Favours first:  diarrhea, elevated serum lipase, epigastric pain, fatty liver, hypertriglyceridemia\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, fatty stools, fever, jaundice, rapid pulse\n\nHypertriglyceridemia-Induced Acute Pancreatitis vs Autoimmune Systemic Vasculitis (e.g., Granulomatosis with Polyangiitis):\n  Favours first:  diarrhea, elevated serum lipase, epigastric pain, fatty liver, hypertriglyceridemia\n  Favours second: abnormal brainstem morphology, abnormal cell morphology, abnormal cerebellum morphology, abnormal conjugate eye movement, abnormal cortical gyration\n\nIdiopathic/Atypical Acute Pancreatitis vs Autoimmune Systemic Vasculitis (e.g., Granulomatosis with Polyangiitis):\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, fatty stools, fever, jaundice, nausea\n  Favours second: abnormal brainstem morphology, abnormal cell morphology, abnormal cerebellum morphology, abnormal conjugate eye movement, abnormal cortical gyration\n\nRelated to Autoimmune Systemic Vasculitis (e.g., Granulomatosis with Polyangiitis): anti-glomerular basement membrane disease, autoimmune disease of cardiovascular system, cogan syndrome\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 55-year-old man presents to the emergency department with chest pain and shortness of breath → pain → Autoimmune Systemic Vasculitis (e.g., Granulomatosis with Polyangiitis)\n  A 55-year-old man presents to the emergency department with chest pain and shortness of breath → limb pain → Autoimmune Systemic Vasculitis (e.g., Granulomatosis with Polyangiitis)"}
